{"format":1,"key":"zone:duskwood","path":"/lore/zone/duskwood","name":"Duskwood","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"duskwood","name":"Duskwood","path":"/lore/zone/duskwood"},"levels":"Levels 18-30","description":"Duskwood lies beneath a curse, its sunlit past hidden by unending gloom. Stormwind has abandoned its human inhabitants, who cling to survival in…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:duskwood","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Duskwood lies beneath a curse, its sunlit past hidden by unending gloom. Stormwind has abandoned its human inhabitants, who cling to survival in Darkshire under the Night Watch's protection. Ghouls, giant venomous spiders, raiding ogres, and savage, mysterious worgen roam its groves and haunted barrows.","Duskwood was once a rich agricultural tract in the Kingdom of Stormwind, with prosperous settlements such as Grand Hamlet and Raven Hill. Its ruin began when Guardian Medivh fell at Karazhan during the First War, unleashing waves of corrupted fel magic that twisted the woodland into a gnarled, shadowy morass. Spiders became terrifying predators, and fleeing wolves spilled north into Elwynn Forest. Grand Hamlet became Darkshire, where terrified townsfolk were left largely to fend for themselves after the royal garrison withdrew to defend the capital.","Commander Althea Ebonlocke and her volunteer militia, the Night Watch, keep Darkshire alive, while Lord Ello Ebonlocke tries to govern the crumbling settlement. Beyond the town's lantern-lit perimeter, danger fills the land. Restless dead raised by the necromancer Morbent Fel stir in massive Raven Hill Cemetery. The Vul'Gol ogres came from Deadwind Pass to claim the south. Dark Riders stalk the crossroads, relentlessly searching for the lost Scythe.","Near Duskwood's center lies a deep, ancient crater untouched by the surrounding corruption: the Twilight Grove. An ancient Great Tree there holds a dormant portal into the Emerald Dream. Soft, ethereal twilight bathes this unearthly sanctuary in the dying land, while sleeping druidic energies watch over it."],"hash":"6934cc","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"d23e9506ab","sec":98},"female-narrator":{"sha":"7361a315fd","sec":107}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Duskwood (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Duskwood_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Duskwood","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Duskwood"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkshire","n":"Darkshire","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/raven-hill-cemetery","n":"Raven Hill Cemetery","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/twilight-grove","n":"Twilight Grove","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/topic/night-watch","n":"Night Watch","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/npc/althea-ebonlocke","n":"Althea Ebonlocke","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/jitters","n":"Jitters","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1043-the-scythe-of-elune","n":"The Scythe of Elune","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/55-morbent-fel","n":"Morbent Fel","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/zone/elwynn","n":"Elwynn Forest","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ridgepoint-tower","n":"Ridgepoint Tower","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/innkeeper-farley","n":"Innkeeper Farley","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dead-acre","n":"Dead Acre","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/addle-s-stead","n":"Addle's Stead","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/beggar-s-haunt","n":"Beggar's Haunt","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/brightwood-grove","n":"Brightwood Grove","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkened-bank","n":"Darkened Bank","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkshire","n":"Darkshire","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkshire-town-hall","n":"Darkshire Town Hall","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dawning-wood-catacombs","n":"Dawning Wood Catacombs","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/forlorn-rowe","n":"Forlorn Rowe","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hushed-bank","n":"Hushed Bank","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/manor-mistmantle","n":"Manor Mistmantle","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lor